# sites-cf833fdbb.kzp -- the probe plan of the perf-sample observer for case C1 on the W3 builds with CF 833fdbb
# (plan/C1_build_manifest.md; the bundle candidates 1df262a and 1b0b338 share this plan: the cited OSAL and
# cFE files are byte-identical in both, and the anchors are resolved per binary by kz anchor).
#
# DATA for `kz anchor` and `kz observe` (format kzp-observe 1, probe/plan/profile.hpp), not the profile
# language of the readiness specification (../*.kzp).  Point sites are named after the Phi sites (role
# sites and call sites), so that `kz replay` maps them.  Source root: a C1 source view (cf/, bp/, osal/,
# cfe/; docs/c1_smoke_observe.md); each sha256 is that of the cited lines, recomputed by kz anchor.
#
# Three files: the executable core-tx (primary) and the shared objects cf.so and bp.so that the start script
# loads (one basis per file: kz anchor --bin, kz observe --basis).  The W3 builds are Release builds
# without a line table: entry/return sites and function-scoped call sites only (the W2 anchor rules: PLT
# calls, refusal of a branch-joined return site).  The tx instance only (PI decision P7 is open): rx runs
# from other files and is not probed.
#
# 2026-10-24 (smoke2): the semaphore name and the ids are read from memory by the kernel's probe-event fetch
# arguments (slots +<offset>(<register>), `string`; kz observe --tracefs), and the points inside OSAL that
# these builds reach by a tail jump (the search of the lookup) or through an inlined helper are entry-reached
# points (func=F enter=G[>H]): the entry of G, kept only where attributed to an open call of F on the same
# thread (docs/observer.md 3.5).
kzp-observe 1
binary core-tx
binary cf.so
binary bp.so

